Package: segmantR
Title: Cell Segmentation for Histology with Human-in-the-Loop Training
Version: 0.1.0.9000
Authors@R:
    person("R.", "Heller", , "raban.heller@charite.de",
           role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0001-8006-9742"))
Description: Cell segmentation for histology and multiplexed tissue imaging.
    Provides classical segmentation methods (adaptive thresholding,
    watershed, Voronoi propagation), wrappers through 'reticulate' for the
    deep learning models 'Cellpose' (Stringer et al. (2021)
    <doi:10.1038/s41592-020-01018-x>), 'StarDist' (Schmidt et al. (2018)
    <doi:10.1007/978-3-030-00934-2_30>) and 'Mesmer' (Greenwald et al.
    (2022) <doi:10.1038/s41587-021-01094-0>), and a human-in-the-loop
    iterative refinement workflow. A 'shiny' application lets researchers
    annotate, correct, train, evaluate and download custom segmentation
    models without leaving R. Versioned declarative segmentation protocols,
    a neutral interchange format (JSON manifests, integer label TIFF,
    GeoJSON, measurement tables with SHA-256 inventories), training dataset
    manifests with grouped splits, and readable 'QuPath' script templates
    with a 'StarDist' parameter adapter support reproducible exchange with
    'QuPath' and partner packages.
